# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored.
# Nothing here is required — with none of it set the app keeps its state in
# files under STATE_DIR and works exactly as it always has.

# Port for the local server (default 4175).
# PORT=4175

# Interface to bind. Defaults to 0.0.0.0, which makes the app reachable from
# other devices on your network — which is the point, if you want the log on
# your phone in the field. There is no authentication, so anyone who can reach
# the port has full read and write access. Set this to restrict it to this
# machine only.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Where files live when the app is not using a bucket. Defaults to the checkout.
# STATE_DIR=/var/lib/tracker

# --- Shared state in an S3 bucket -------------------------------------------
#
# Unset, the app keeps its state in files under STATE_DIR. Name a bucket and it
# keeps them there instead, which is what lets the laptop and the phone be the
# same log rather than two diverging ones: every write is conditional on the
# version it read, so an instance whose copy has gone stale is refused rather
# than allowed to overwrite whoever got there first.
#
# Photographs go in the bucket too, under <prefix>/photos/. The local photos/
# directory becomes a cache — the bucket is the truth, but a photograph already
# looked at still draws with no signal.
#
# Turn on bucket versioning. Deletes then leave a marker rather than destroying
# bytes, so a photograph the orphan sweep took by mistake is recoverable.
#
# The bucket holds nothing but your log. Keep it private: there is no
# authentication in front of it or in front of the app.
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_PREFIX=fieldnotes
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=

# The IAM user needs, on arn:aws:s3:::<bucket>/<prefix>/*
#   s3:GetObject  s3:PutObject  s3:DeleteObject
# and on arn:aws:s3:::<bucket>
#   s3:ListBucket
# ListBucket is not optional. Without it S3 reports an object that simply is
# not there as denied rather than absent, so a fresh bucket is indistinguishable
# from bad credentials and the seed never runs — and the orphan sweep cannot
# enumerate photographs at all.

# Only for an S3-compatible store that is not AWS — Cloudflare R2, MinIO. Set
# it and requests go path-style to that host instead of to AWS.
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
